<p>Today is the last day of published green rates for this confirmation period. On the basis of exchange rats from 23-31 January 1997, the average UK RMG is below +5 per cent, at +4.448 per cent and will therefore exit confirmation on 2 February. There will then be a shortened reference period running from 2 - 10 February before normal reference periods resume on 11 February. All other green rates are currently forecast to remain unchanged from 2 February. With the resumption of reference periods, the 3-day (6 per cent) rule will come back into force.</p>
